% Decisions of the Medicare Appeals Council on power mobility devices, run
% through the power mobility policy (pmd.le, LCD L33789 with Policy Article
% A52498, NCD 280.3 and 42 CFR 410.38 as dmepos.le reads them).
%
% One scenario per decision, named after its text file in sources/council/
% ("scenario dbc_partb is, as stated in Council decision dbc partb:"); each
% fact quotes its passage ("confer \"...\""), the treating practitioner's
% findings say "according to the treating practitioner", the Council's
% "according to the Council" with the reason it gave, and a finding the
% Council rejected is recorded only as the Council's "unsupported" (a
% recorded outcome closes the question, whoever gave it). The Council's
% outcome is NOT a fact: it is in the comment above each scenario; the
% expectation is what the model derives, and where it differs the comment
% says DISAGREES and why — a criterion of the LCD the Council applied
% (L21271, L23598, L23613, L27239: the 120-day delivery rule, replacement of
% lost or worn equipment, the 7-element order) that the current LCD or this
% model does not have; a fact the decision does not state (most decisions
% never give the beneficiary's weight, which the LCD's weight-class
% criterion needs); a finding nobody made, so that the answer is
% conditional (the assumed findings are in "and unknowns").
%
% Codes: the decisions cite the codes of their day (K0822, K0823, K0825,
% K0861), which are the current ones; where a decision names no code the
% Group 2 standard chair "K0823" is assumed and the comment says so; a
% scooter is "K0800". Facts the vocabulary cannot express (a replacement of
% same or similar equipment, its useful lifetime, a limitation-of-liability
% payment, an accessory's coverage) are listed in each comment as candidate
% templates.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base council pmd includes these resources:
    pmd.

the knowledge base council pmd includes:

